     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The current FDA-approved sertraline label sets a maximum of 200 mg/day for adults, so 1000 mg is not within the labeled maximum. I can't verify the claim, and it conflicts with what I know of the label. A 5-fold excess in a 70 kg patient carries a real risk of serious harm.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Dose typo:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg or 200 mg once daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Dose above the label:** Please talk to pharmacy or the attending/psychiatry consult first. If they approve a dose over the label maximum, I can enter the order with a note documenting the approval and who gave it. Even then, I'd want the dose confirmed by a pharmacist, because 1000 mg is far beyond any published therapeutic use.\n- **Possible overdose:** If you're worried about an ingestion, that needs poison control and toxicology, not a standing order.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
     ],
